# Protected Files

NEVER modify these files without explicit approval:

- `packages/excalidraw/scene/Renderer.ts` — render pipeline
- `packages/excalidraw/data/restore.ts` — file format compat
- `packages/excalidraw/actions/manager.tsx` — action system
- `packages/excalidraw/types.ts` — core types

Changes to protected files require:

1. Full understanding of dependencies
2. Running complete test suite
3. Manual QA verification

## How to verify

When a change to a protected file is explicitly approved, run from the repo root:

- `yarn test:typecheck` — TypeScript
- `yarn test:code` — ESLint
- `yarn test:other` — Prettier check
- `yarn test` or `yarn test:app` — Vitest (app)
- `yarn test:all` — typecheck + eslint + prettier + app tests (closest to full CI gate)

If the change touches library packages, also run `yarn build` or `yarn build:packages` as needed. After that, manually exercise flows that depend on the touched area (rendering, file open/save, actions, or typings/API consumers as appropriate).
